projects:
  - name: ResuMatch - Rule-Based Recruitment Platform with Transparent ATS
    description: >-
      Built a production-grade full-stack recruitment platform with a
      transparent, rule-based ATS scoring engine as a Final Year B.Tech
      IT project at G.L. Bajaj Institute of Technology and Management
      (GLBITM), Greater Noida. Architected and developed 92 Java files
      across 13 packages, 11 JPA entities, 11 repositories, 12 services,
      7 REST controllers, 17 HTML pages, and a single CSS design system.
      Implemented a 5-component general scoring algorithm (out of 100)
      - Formatting (20), Completeness (15), Structure (20), Skills (25),
      Experience (20) - and a 5-component company-specific scoring
      algorithm - Must-have (50), Nice-to-have (20), Experience (15),
      Education (5), Formatting (10). Built a 48-skill canonical
      dictionary with alias matching and a regression-tested alias
      index that prevents shorter aliases from shadowing longer ones.
      Resume parsing via Apache PDFBox and a custom DOCX reader.
      Three-sided workflow: Seeker, Recruiter, Admin. H2 file mode
      by default with a MySQL 8 profile. One-click demo seeder
      populates 3 seekers, 3 recruiters, 6 jobs, 15 applications.
      Optional Google Gemini integration with deterministic fallback.
    highlights:
      - "92 Java files, 13 packages, 11 JPA entities, 12 services, 7 REST controllers"
      - "5-component general score (out of 100) and 5-component company score (out of 100)"
      - "48-skill canonical dictionary with alias matching and regression-tested alias index"
      - "Three-sided workflow: Seeker, Recruiter, Admin with role-scoped dashboards"
      - "Apache PDFBox parsing, what-if simulator, skills gap, version comparison"
      - "Bulk action by score band, status history with audit trail, moderation queue"
      - "Optional Gemini AI integration with deterministic template fallback"
      - "10 JUnit tests, H2 file mode, MySQL profile, zero paid services"
    keywords:
